#[doc = r#"This message is a request to cancel an Action which has been allocated and planned.  A planning input such as Effect, Action, Task and DMPI can't easily be canceled or removed from the System due to race conditions between their various users and publishers, inevitability of the associated activity, etc.  Additionally, the operator or service initiating the cancellation might be different than the one that manages RequirementSets and/or issues *PlanCommand, introducing additional race conditions.  In order to avoid race conditions, receive positive feedback on the success of the cancellation and allow canceled messages/objects to remain in the system for historical purposes, an explicit ActionCancelCommand is necessary.  An ActionCancelCommand shall result in the Action being canceled unless execution was already inevitable.  If the Action was inevitable and started executing but can be stopped (such as a long collection Action) it shall cancel as soon as possible.  ActionCancelCommand shall result in managers of RequirementSets to remove the associated Action, thereby removing the Action from the next planning cycle.  Services other than those that manage RequirementSets and execute activities aren't required to handle ActionCancelCommand.  ActionCancelCommand doesn't necessarily trigger a replan (there isn't a corresponding planning trigger), therefore a System could continue to navigate routes related to the canceled Action, even though the Action won't occur.  A subsequent replan could exclude the Action.  Status or feedback for this message is given through ActionCancelCommandStatus but the resulting status of the Action is given through ActionStatus.UCI_PRIMITIVE: Command-2."#]
