#[doc = r#"This message commands an ActivityPlan related planning function/action.  Example planning functions include updating an existing ActivityPlan, creating a new ActivityPlan or combining/stitching existing ActivityPlans together.  The command includes many inputs to the planning function while others may come from a variety of other messages.  The expected output of the planning function is an ActivityPlan message.
The command includes options for constraining the planning function in a variety of ways using existing plans of the same type or by other plan types.  For example, an ActivityPlan could be constrained by a previous ActivityPlan and/or a TaskPlan.
The command includes environment overrides to selectively modify details of the current planning environment in the context of a single planning command. For example, a known threat Entity in the environment could be removed and an expected Entity could be for added to the environment in the context of a single planning command in support of speculative or "what-if"  contingency planning.
The command includes settings for "weightings" that influence the decisions of operators or planning algorithms performing the planning.UCI_PRIMITIVE: Command-2."#]
