#[doc = r#"This message is a request to cancel an Effect which has been allocated and planned.  A planning input such as Effect, Action, Task and DMPI can't easily be canceled or removed from the System due to race conditions between their various users and publishers, inevitability of the associated activity, etc.  Additionally, the operator or service initiating the cancellation might be different than the one that manages RequirementSets and/or issues *PlanCommand, introducing additional race conditions.  In order to avoid race conditions, receive positive feedback on the success of the cancellation and allow canceled messages/objects to remain in the system for historical purposes, an explicit EffectCancelCommand is necessary.  An EffectCancelCommand shall result in the Effect being canceled unless execution was already inevitable.  If the Effect was inevitable and started executing but can be stopped (such as a long collection Effect) it shall cancel as soon as possible.  EffectCancelCommand shall result in managers of RequirementSets to remove the associated Effect, thereby removing the Effect from the next planning cycle.  Services other than those that manage RequirementSets and execute activities aren't required to handle EffectCancelCommand.  EffectCancelCommand doesn't necessarily trigger a replan (there isn't a corresponding planning trigger), therefore a System could continue to navigate routes related to the canceled Effect, even though the Effect won't occur.  A subsequent replan could exclude the Effect.  Status or feedback for this message is given through EffectCancelCommandStatus but the resulting status of the Effect is given through EffectStatus.UCI_PRIMITIVE: Command-2."#]
