#[doc = r#"This message specifies the Effects allocated to a System.  Allocation can be done manually by operators, by an allocation service or a combination.  This message decouples Effect allocation from kinematic, action and other types of planning; Effect allocations can be created, updated and approved independent of other *Plans.  It enables any type of *Plan to be a constraint on Effect allocation.    
An EffectPlan can be an input and/or output of planning processes.  For example the EffectPlan for the top System in a hierarchical System of System could be an input to an Effect allocation service that the produces an EffectPlan per subordinate System with their subset of allocated Effects.
Additional details such as timing, dependencies, decomposition, etc. can be added during the Effect allocation process and captured in the EffectPlan to supplement the information in the allocated Effects themselves.
An EffectPlan can be created discretely or as part of a MissionPlan that includes other *Plans.  An EffectPlan can only be activated and executed as part of a MissionPlan.  A MissionPlan can be used to plan the execution order of multiple EffectPlans and *Plans in general.  An EffectPlan can be subject to approval per Approval* messages.  Planning, approval, activation and execution state information for an EffectPlan are given in other EffectPlan* messages.UCI_PRIMITIVE: Data-1."#]
