#[doc = r#"This message represents what is commonly referred to as the two line element (TLE) for an Entity in orbit around Earth.  It describes a satellite's orbit kinematics using general perturbations theory (SGP, SGP4, PPT3) and Keplerian elements.  An orbital element set (OES), or simply "el set", contains six classical orbital elements and a time element (epoch) which can be converted into position and velocity vectors to generate the geometry and motion of where the satellite is located and where it is going.  An OES is a refined collection of data, continually updated over the life of the satellite.  Single position kinematics, ephemeris and VCM for an Entity are given in other Entity* messages.  Placing Entity-related data into separate messages enables separate sources/services to report data for the same Entity instance.   For example, an identity fusion service could publish the base Entity message to establish the existence of a battlespace object and other kinematic fusion and/or kinematic propagation services could publish Entity kinematics at higher rates and in different reference frames without resending the base Entity data that did not change.UCI_PRIMITIVE: Data-1."#]
