#[doc = r#"This message defines a Response to triggering event or events. It is effectively a Requirement to "be ready to" 1) instantiate and plan a Requirement (Effect, Action, Task or [Capability]Command tailored to the triggering even, 2) activate a previously created *Plan, 3) issue an alert, 4) do nothing. Responsibility for the Response can be allocated/assigned to a System via a ResponsePlan that is part of a MissionPlan. In other words, ResponsePlans allow Responses to be delegated across a SoS. Activating a ResponsePlan activates monitoring of the triggering events for each of its Responses. A Response is executing whenever its triggering events are being monitored. An executing Response causes no changes to the Mission unless a triggering event occurs. When a triggering event occurs, the options within the Response are evaluated, potentially leading to selection and instantiation of one or options within the Response.

***********************
For Planned C2, evaluating a Response option based on Requirements or *Plans generally means evaluating whole *Plans. To evaluate a Response option it is generally necessary to create, update, validate, assess and/or score *Plans that include it. Selecting and activating a Response option generally means approving and activating a *Plan that includes it.
***********************

A Response can continue to execute (triggering events can continue to be monitored) after a Response option has been initiated. An instantiation of a Response option is detailed in the ResponseActivity message. Response can be manually initiated via the ResponseCommand message.UCI_PRIMITIVE: Data-1."#]
