#[doc = r#"This message invokes a MissionPlan planning process.  Each planning process is declared with a unique ID in the ControlStatus message; that ID is used in this message to invoke the process.  A MissionPlan is an aggregation of other *Plan types, therefore MissionPlanCommand planning processes (and this message) can result in multiple *Plan types/messages.  This message includes many inputs to the planning process but many others may come from a variety of other messages.  A few examples of the many inputs include:
1. Options for constraining the planning function in a variety of ways using existing Plans of the same type or by other Plan types.  For example, a MissionPlan could be constrained by a previous RoutePlan, a previous RouteActivityPlan and/or a TaskPlan.
2. Environment overrides to selectively modify details of the current planning environment in the context of a single planning command. For example, a known threat Entity in the environment could be removed and an expected Entity could be added to the environment in the context of a single planning command in support of "what-if" planning.
3. "Weightings" that influence the decisions of operators or planning algorithms performing the planning.
4. Temporal and/or kinematic begin and end points.UCI_PRIMITIVE: Command-2."#]
