#[doc = r#"This message specifies planned activities for a System with an OrbitPlan.  An "Orbit Activity" is any *Capability-related activity planned in context of the kinematic OrbitPlan of the System.  Activities are the planned implementation details of Effects, Actions, Tasks, Capability Commands, etc.  Orbit activity planning can be done manually by operators, by an activity planning service or a combination.  This message decouples activity planning from allocation, kinematic and other types of planning; the OrbitActivityPlan of a System can be created, updated and approved independent of other *Plans.  It enables any type of *Plan to be a constraint on activity planning.
An OrbitActivityPlan can be an input and/or output of planning processes.  For example an OrbitActivityPlan from a previous round of planning could be an input to an activity planning service that adds additional planned activities to it.
A single System can have multiple independent OrbitActivityPlans for different Task, Capability, sensor, etc. types; that are developed by one or more services across a multi-System service oriented architecture; at different times then independently updated and approved.  Optionally, all types of activities for a System can be included in a single OrbitActivityPlan.
An OrbitActivityPlan can be created discretely or as part of a MissionPlan that includes other *Plans.  An OrbitActivityPlan can only be activated and executed as part of a MissionPlan.  A MissionPlan can be used to plan the execution order of multiple OrbitActivityPlans and *Plans in general.  An OrbitActivityPlan can be subject to approval per Approval* messages.  Planning, approval, activation and execution state information for an OrbitActivityPlan are given in other OrbitActivityPlan* messages.UCI_PRIMITIVE: Data-1."#]
