#[doc = r#"This message indicates the default system rules for determining at which classification a product should be labeled.  Classification labeling of a products can happen in 3 ways.
    
1.) Classification is specified as part of the collection task.  This method is used to tell the sensor subsystem to label the product with classification as part of product creation.  When this method is used, the Product Classification Plan can be used to determine the classification of the collection task based on the filter criteria such as zone or time.

2.) The operator creates a Product Classification Task to perform post-collect, post-download classification (or reclassification) of a product.  With this method, the operator can choose to classify based on the Product Classification Plan or can override the plan by specifying a classification.

3.) The classification of a product generated from product processing does not directly use this plan to determine classification.  The default behavior would be for the processing function to classify the new product with the highest classification of the new product's parent products.  The operator has the ability to override this default behavior using the ProcessingTask and ProcessingRequest messages.  If any post-creation classification/reclassification of processed products is desired, method 2 described above should be utilized.UCI_PRIMITIVE: Data-1."#]
