#[doc = r#"This message has 2 uses.
Message use 1:

This message is a request that a product be classified at a particular level.

A Product Classification Request directly invokes classification service functionality to classify/reclassify a product.  Execution of the classification request would result in a Product Classification Request Status followed by a Product Classification Report.

There are 2 ways this message can be generated.  1.) By the operator to command immediate reclassification of a product.  2.) Automated by a service as a result of execution of a Classification Task.

When specifying a Classification Request, the user can choose to utilize the Product Classification Plan to determine classification or can override the plan by specifying a classification.

If automatically generated as a result of Classification Task execution, the classification requirements would be populated with those specified in the Classification Task.  This allows the default plan to be utilized or overridden on a task by task basis.

Message use 2:

This message requests that a classification label is generated per the Product Classification Plan and returned in the Product Classification Request Status.  When the message is used in this way, the classification should be omitted from the Classification Requirements.  This message use allows for a service decomposition where the service applying the classification label is separate from the service that determines classification based on the classification plan.UCI_PRIMITIVE: ActionRequest-2."#]
