#[doc = r#"This message specifies the Tasks allocated to a System.  Allocation can be done manually by operators, by an allocation service or a combination.  This message decouples Task allocation from kinematic, action and other types of planning; Tasks allocations can be created, updated and approved independent of other *Plans.  It enables any type of *Plan to be a constraint on task allocation.

A TaskPlan can be an input and/or output of planning processes.  For example the TaskPlan for the top System in a hierarchical System of System could be an input to a task allocation service that the produces a TaskPlan per subordinate System with their subset of allocated Tasks.

Additional details such as timing, dependencies, decomposition, etc. can be added during the task allocation process and captured in the TaskPlan to supplement the information in the allocated Tasks themselves.

A TaskPlan can be created discretely or as part of a MissionPlan that includes other *Plans.  A TaskPlan can only be activated and executed as part of a MissionPlan.  A MissionPlan can be used to plan the execution order of multiple TaskPlans and *Plans in general.  A TaskPlan can be subject to approval per Approval* messages.  Planning, approval, activation and execution state information for a TaskPlan are given in other TaskPlan* messages.UCI_PRIMITIVE: Data-1."#]
